      "_id": "6a5361cef8aa38c957de12ff",
      "title": "Finding Focus In A Noisy Season",
      "slug": "finding-focus-in-a-noisy-season",
      "description": "How I simplified my days, protected attention, and learned to finish what mattered.",
      "excerpt": "",
      "body": "<h2>Attention is a home</h2><p>When everything was asking for a response, I began by choosing what deserved one. Focus was not about doing more. It was about refusing to spend my best energy on every passing urgency.</p><p>I built a simple rule: one important task before noise. That small habit changed the shape of my mornings.</p>",
      "coverImage": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1455390582262-044cdead277a?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80",
